Decode the casing and normalization mapping tables without a record overlay

VSS.Implementation.UCD_Casing_UTF8 and UCD_Normalization_UTF8 keep their
mapping information as 32-bit (casing) and 64-bit (normalization) words with
the fields at fixed bit positions, counting from the least significant bit, and
then overlay an array of a record on the raw table (Simplified_Mapping_Data_
Table, Contextual_Mapping_Data_Table, Mapping_Data_Table).  The records place
their fields with "at 0 range N .. M", which follows the bit and byte order of
the machine, so the overlay reads the right fields only on little-endian
targets: it is the same mistake as in the Unicode core data table (see
ucd-endianness.patch).

On big-endian s390x the offsets and counts come out wrong.  The first visible
effect is a Constraint_Error in Unchecked_Append (range check at
vss-implementation-utf8_strings-mutable_operations.adb:700, from => 18562) for
any lower- or upper-casing, which killed ada_language_server at start-up
(elaboration of lsp-ada_configurations.adb:43 lower-cases a string); the
normalization forms (NFC, NFD, NFKC, NFKD) return garbage or raise.

Decode the raw word with shifts and masks in the three functions that read the
tables (Get_Contextual_Case_Mapping_Information,
Get_Simplified_Case_Mapping_Information, Get_Decomposition_Information).  The
result is the same on every machine, and on little-endian targets it is
unchanged.  Checked on s390x with the transformers of VSS.Transformers.Casing
and .Normalization on 13 cases (ASCII and accented lower/upper case, final
sigma, sharp s, NFC/NFD/NFKC/NFKD of an accented letter, a ligature and Hangul):
12 failed before, all pass now.

--- a/source/text/implementation/vss-implementation-utf8_casing.adb
+++ b/source/text/implementation/vss-implementation-utf8_casing.adb
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 
 with VSS.Implementation.Strings;
 with VSS.Implementation.UCD_Casing;
+with Interfaces;
 with VSS.Implementation.UTF8_Strings.Mutable_Operations;
 
 package body VSS.Implementation.UTF8_Casing is
@@ -437,6 +438,7 @@
    is
       use type VSS.Implementation.UCD_Casing_UTF8.Mapping_Data_Offset;
       use type VSS.Unicode.Code_Point;
+      use type Interfaces.Unsigned_32;
 
       Group  : constant VSS.Implementation.UCD_Casing_UTF8.Mapping_Group :=
         VSS.Implementation.UCD_Casing_UTF8.Mapping_Group
@@ -446,10 +448,42 @@
           VSS.Implementation.UCD_Casing_UTF8.Mapping_Data_Offset
             (Code mod VSS.Implementation.UCD_Casing_UTF8.Mapping_Group_Size);
 
+      Raw : constant Interfaces.Unsigned_32 :=
+        VSS.Implementation.UCD_Casing_UTF8.Mapping_Data_Table_Raw
+          (Mapping (Group) + Offset);
+
+      function Field (Low, Width : Natural) return Natural is
+        (Natural (Interfaces.Shift_Right (Raw, Low) and (2 ** Width - 1)));
+
+      function Flag (Pos : Natural) return Boolean is (Field (Pos, 1) = 1);
+      --  The table holds 32-bit words with the fields at fixed bit positions,
+      --  least significant bit first (see the representation clause of the
+      --  record).  Decode them here instead of overlaying the record on the
+      --  table: the overlay follows the machine's bit and byte order, so on a
+      --  big-endian target (s390x) it gives wrong offsets and counts.
+
    begin
       return
-        VSS.Implementation.UCD_Casing_UTF8.Contextual_Mapping_Data_Table
-          (Mapping (Group) + Offset);
+        (Offset         =>
+           VSS.Implementation.UCD_Casing_UTF8.Casing_UTF8_Data_Offset
+             (Field (0, 15)),
+         Length         =>
+           VSS.Implementation.UCD_Casing_UTF8
+             .Contextual_Casing_Character_Count
+             (Field (16, 2)),
+         Count          =>
+           VSS.Implementation.UCD_Casing_UTF8
+             .Contextual_Casing_UTF8_Code_Unit_Count (Field (24, 3)),
+         Context_Change =>
+           (Enter_Final_Sigma          => Flag (18),
+            Continue_Final_Sigma       => Flag (19),
+            Enter_After_Soft_Dotted    => Flag (20),
+            Continue_After_Soft_Dotted => Flag (21),
+            Enter_After_I              => Flag (22),
+            Continue_After_I           => Flag (23)),
+         Cased          => Flag (28),
+         Case_Ignorable => Flag (29),
+         Changes        => Flag (31));
    end Get_Contextual_Case_Mapping_Information;
 
